1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,390
In two weeks, saying hello to Voyager 1
再过两周，跟旅行者一号说声“你好”，

2
00:00:02,390 --> 00:00:03,960
takes a full day to arrive.
要等整整一天才到。

3
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:04,590
Its reply?
它回一句？

4
00:00:04,590 --> 00:00:06,990
Another day. Two days for one hello.
再等一天。一声你好，来回两天。

5
00:00:06,990 --> 00:00:08,190
On November eighteenth,
十一月十八日，

6
00:00:08,190 --> 00:00:10,550
Voyager 1 reaches one light day from Earth.
旅行者一号离地球一光日。

7
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:13,090
That is about twenty six billion kilometers,
大约二百六十亿公里，

8
00:00:13,090 --> 00:00:14,650
or sixteen billion miles.
也就是一百六十亿英里。

9
00:00:14,650 --> 00:00:16,860
It made the Hacker News front page this week,
这周它上了 Hacker News 首页，

10
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:18,500
and everyone is doing the math.
网友都在算这道题。

11
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:19,580
Today's brain teaser:
今天的烧脑问题：

12
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:22,530
why does a call take a day, and how do we even hear it?
打个电话凭啥要等一天？我们又是怎么听见的？

13
00:00:22,530 --> 00:00:23,870
Meet our hero, Voyager 1,
认识主角：旅行者一号，

14
00:00:23,870 --> 00:00:25,870
launched in nineteen seventy seven.
一九七七年出发。

15
00:00:25,870 --> 00:00:27,630
Forty nine years on the road.
在路上四十九年，

16
00:00:27,630 --> 00:00:28,600
Still talking.
还在说话。

17
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:30,910
Twist one: the slow part is not Voyager.
反转一：慢的不是旅行者，

18
00:00:30,910 --> 00:00:31,720
It is light.
是光。

19
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:33,540
Light is the fastest thing there is:
光是最快的东西：

20
00:00:33,540 --> 00:00:35,840
three hundred thousand kilometers a second.
每秒三十万公里。

21
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:37,890
Sunlight takes eight minutes to reach us.
太阳光到地球要八分钟，

22
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:39,670
Moonlight takes about one second.
月光只要一秒多。

23
00:00:39,670 --> 00:00:41,050
A radio wave is light too,
无线电也是光，

24
00:00:41,050 --> 00:00:42,920
so it obeys the same speed limit.
一样被这个限速卡住。

25
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:44,330
A new phone will not help.
换手机、换套餐，

26
00:00:44,330 --> 00:00:45,910
Neither will a better plan.
都没用。

27
00:00:45,910 --> 00:00:49,000
Voyager itself flies about seventeen kilometers a second.
旅行者自己每秒飞十七公里，

28
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,400
That is sixty thousand kilometers an hour.
一小时六万公里。

29
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:51,660
Fast?
快吗？

30
00:00:51,660 --> 00:00:54,600
Light is still about seventeen thousand times faster.
光还是比它快一万七千多倍。

31
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:56,050
So it took forty nine years
所以它飞了四十九年，

32
00:00:56,050 --> 00:00:57,570
to get one light day away.
才走出一光日。

33
00:00:57,570 --> 00:00:59,190
Twist two: Voyager whispers.
反转二：旅行者说话像耳语，

34
00:00:59,190 --> 00:01:01,280
Its radio uses about twenty watts.
电台功率大约二十瓦。

35
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:03,370
NASA compares that to a fridge light bulb,
NASA 说，差不多一个冰箱灯泡，

36
00:01:03,370 --> 00:01:05,130
shouting across the solar system.
却要喊过整个太阳系。

37
00:01:05,130 --> 00:01:06,400
And the farther it goes,
而且越远，

38
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:07,900
the fainter it gets, fast.
声音弱得越快。

39
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:09,310
Picture a can of spray paint.
想象一罐喷漆往外喷，

40
00:01:09,310 --> 00:01:11,770
The paint spreads over a bigger and bigger ball.
漆铺在一个越来越大的球面上。

41
00:01:11,770 --> 00:01:12,530
Twice as far,
远一倍，

42
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:13,750
four times fainter.
就弱四倍。

43
00:01:13,750 --> 00:01:14,980
So how do we hear it?
那怎么听见？

44
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:16,030
With giant ears.
靠巨大的耳朵。

45
00:01:16,030 --> 00:01:17,520
NASA's Deep Space Network
NASA 的深空网，

46
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:19,560
uses dishes seventy meters wide.
天线锅七十米宽。

47
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:22,770
One in California, one in Spain, one in Australia,
加州、西班牙、澳大利亚各一处，

48
00:01:22,770 --> 00:01:25,900
so as Earth spins, one always faces deep space.
地球怎么转，总有一个朝着深空。

49
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:27,390
The dish gathers that whisper
大锅收集那一丝耳语，

50
00:01:27,390 --> 00:01:28,840
like a bowl catching rain.
就像大碗接雨。

51
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:32,290
Twist three, the most mind bending: one light day sounds far,
反转三，最烧脑：一光日听着很远，

52
00:01:32,290 --> 00:01:33,540
but it is next door.
其实就在家门口。

53
00:01:33,540 --> 00:01:35,910
The nearest star is over four light years away.
最近的恒星在四光年开外，

54
00:01:35,910 --> 00:01:38,300
That is more than fifteen hundred light days.
也就是一千五百多光日。

55
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:40,080
At Voyager's speed, going that far
按旅行者的速度飞过去，

56
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:43,230
would take about seventy five thousand years, by our math.
我们算了算，要七万五千年。

57
00:01:43,230 --> 00:01:45,430
And Voyager is not even aimed at that star.
而且它根本不是朝那颗星飞的，

58
00:01:45,430 --> 00:01:47,450
It is just drifting through the dark.
只是在黑暗里漂。

59
00:01:47,450 --> 00:01:49,600
In twenty twelve it left the Sun's bubble,
二零一二年，它飞出了太阳的“泡泡”，

60
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:51,500
the first spacecraft ever to do it.
是第一个做到的飞船。

61
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:52,650
Its power keeps fading,
它的电越来越少，

62
00:01:52,650 --> 00:01:54,770
so NASA keeps switching instruments off.
NASA 只能一台台关掉仪器。

63
00:01:54,770 --> 00:01:57,580
In April twenty twenty six, one more went quiet,
二零二六年四月，又关掉一台，

64
00:01:57,580 --> 00:01:58,580
to save energy.
为了省电。

65
00:01:58,580 --> 00:02:02,320
Fine print: the date and distance come from EarthSky, using NASA data.
友情提示：日期和距离来自 EarthSky 根据 NASA 的数据；

66
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:05,270
Seventy five thousand years is our own math on paper.
七万五千年是我们在纸上算的。

67
00:02:05,270 --> 00:02:06,570
Voyager 2 is behind it.
旅行者二号在后面追，

68
00:02:06,570 --> 00:02:09,560
It reaches one light day around twenty thirty five.
大约二零三五年到一光日。

69
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:11,090
So why does the call take a day?
所以电话凭啥要等一天？

70
00:02:11,090 --> 00:02:13,300
Because even light needs a day to get there.
因为连光都要走一天。

71
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:14,460
And how do we hear it?
我们怎么听见？

72
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:16,630
With giant ears, and a lot of patience.
靠大耳朵，还有耐心。

73
00:02:16,630 --> 00:02:18,190
Next time a text feels slow,
下次嫌消息回得慢，

74
00:02:18,190 --> 00:02:21,910
think of Voyager. It waits a whole day, and still says hello.
想想旅行者：等一天，还在说你好。

